The mark verifying authorities' root certificates a Verified Mark Certificate must chain to,
as PEM blocks. Text outside the blocks, like this, is ignored.

None is here yet. Each is to be added from its authority's own repository, with its SHA-256
fingerprint checked against a second source and written above its block. Until one is, no
logo is shown unless the user adds roots in `bimi-roots.pem` in the config directory.
